        <mxCell id="q9VUOO2rpJe4aaUoL2ZS-36" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Dealership V3&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;It should CRUD Client, Car and Sale. When a Sales happen, it should send a sales notification to a lambda that will processes the sale and create a&amp;nbsp; invoice. The invoice should be saved to a S3 Bucket that will generate a event and this event should be consumed by a lambda and the lambda should send a e-mail to the client.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The authentication should be in the API Gateway, through Amazon Cognito or using an lambda authorizer. (In study).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In this version, the Client and Car APIs will send a event to the Client/Car Created Topic, so that a Lambda process it and saves it in the Sales database. In this way, the Sales API will not have to call the Client and Car databases, decreasing the SLA.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="q9VUOO2rpJe4aaUoL2ZS-9">
          <mxGeometry x="930" y="20" width="610" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
